I chose a small negative gain on cart position (‑0.5) to push left when the cart drifts right, and a relatively strong negative gain on pole angle (‑4.5) so that the controller reacts promptly to any lean: a positive angle produces a right‑ward force and a negative angle produces a left‑ward force. The cart‑velocity gain (‑0.2) and angular‑velocity gain (‑1.5) add damping to both translational and rotational motion, helping to suppress oscillations without driving the force into saturation. The bias is set to zero to avoid introducing a constant drift bias. All weights stay within the allowed ‑6.0 → 6.0 range, keeping typical actions inside the ±3 N actuator limits while providing the feedback structure needed for long‑duration balancing.
