The highest rewards so far all use the maximum angle weight (6) and a modest bias term. I keep those constants and make small adjustments to the remaining weights: a slightly positive cart‑position weight (0.2) to pull the cart back toward zero, a less aggressive negative velocity weight (‑0.1) to provide gentle damping without over‑correcting, and increase the angular‑velocity gain to 3.0 for stronger compensation of pole swing. The bias remains zero to avoid systematic drift. This combination should reduce cart‑position drift while preserving strong pole‑angle correction, likely extending episode length beyond the current best (≈274).
