The weight on cart position is made slightly negative to generate a restoring force opposite to the cart’s displacement, thereby counteracting the monotonic drift observed in the best prior policies. The pole‑angle weight remains at the high value 6 to provide strong corrective torque based on tilt. The cart‑velocity coefficient stays at -0.5 for damping translational speed, while the angular‑velocity term at 2.3 supplies moderate correction of pole‑rate. No bias term is added, keeping the controller low‑energy and minimizing constant offsets. This combination aims to maintain angular stability while preventing lateral drift, targeting longer episode lengths and higher cumulative reward.
